Sorry if this question is covered somewhere obvious. I have inherited some Argos doppler and GPS data that I am using for a spatial analysis on Clark's nutcrackers (bird). To my knowledge, no calibration was performed for the transmitters before they were deployed. For the GPS data, I have the fix type (2D or 3D) and for the Doppler data, I have the error ellipse information, including GDOP values (in mHz). Can I perform any kind of opportunistic calibration using these values, other values provided by Argos that I have not listed, or calibration data from an unrelated project as a better-than-nothing measure? Thanks in advance, I am very new to spatial analysis and can use all the help I can get.

