If you are concerned about these, you can annotate the points in your suspect models by color to see if the track moves to a different place over time. A bell-shaped variogram could indicate a seasonal migration with two distinct seasonal ranges, and a sharp upward tail at the end could indicate an abrupt shift in a home range well into a movement track, so I would check for these situations in particular.

Jesse

