I concur with Jesse. At the end where the variogram shoots up, the CIs also become very wide. You can still imagine an asymptote running through the CIs. The errors in variograms (and ACF and MSD) are correlated, so trends that can fit within the CIs aren't necessarily meaningful.

You will also get a better sense when you fit models to the data and compare the empirical variograms to the theoretical variograms.

Best,
Chris

