Hi Ryan,

This is the approach that I would recommend for the moment. Especially for the perching data, I would make sure there is sufficient time between the different perches for the stationary model to make sense. There are some other posts on this topic in the group.
Generally, I would validate with block cross validation. I haven't yet made good working easy to use tools for this task, but Fieberg has a paper on RSF diagnostic plots.
Not yet and if both the selection and movement parameters change per behavior, I'm not sure that there would be much more to squeeze out of the data with a fully non-stationary model. (Similar, with an SSF with behavioral states in it.)

Best,
Chris

